{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791597313,"nonce":"nFodEg48tt/WweoiCv4XNYosxUI=","message":"cn tabs content moved onto it in 2cbf0bff (for_each and show now take a signal, state, computed or plain value, f883d9cf; class layers apply position, 5de9e647). The selected panel is the one row; with a transition the old panel stays mounted, out of flow (class_when cn-tabs-panel--leaving, a per-row signal its start sets), until its motion's exit is done.\n\nFindings:\n- MotionHandle::exit only queues the exit for the next render frame, so done is first asked one frame after start. The old stateful code asked right after exit() and so probably never showed the exit animation; the new code should. Not observed in a running app: the headless tests have no paint pass, so the exit finishes at once there.\n- Updates a row's start queues are applied in the pass that starts it, so the leaving class takes the old panel out of flow in the same frame as the new panel appears.\n- Class layers did not apply position (only inset); they do now.\n- Known limit: A to B to A within one exit animation builds a second panel for A under the same motion key as the one still leaving, so the two share motion state. The old code could not hit it (one panel per tab at a time).\n- Two tests that passed by luck of ordering were fixed: class_when scenes left bindings behind for the next test's tree (it failed when run serially), and the DSL cn_tabs harness frame did not apply property updates.\n\nRemaining cn Stateful sites: sidebar, tree, select, combobox, pagination, navigation_menu, dropdown_menu, resizable, number_input, input_otp, collapsible, accordion, slider, popover.","files":null}]}